
============================================================================================
LRC(14) ALTERNATING CUSP SEQUENCE ATLAS S15
============================================================================================
Goal: expose the recursive integer/fractional sequences behind large absolute cusp mass but tiny signed mass.

============================================================================================
RESIDUE COEFFICIENT SIGN INVENTORY
============================================================================================
C_d(r) is the finite mod-7 coefficient in K(n_1,...,n_6,0,...)=C_d(n mod 7)/(n_1...n_6).
Individual C_d(r) are complex, so the signed real atoms are conjugate pairs r and -r.  The table compares the signed paired total with the all-positive paired total.  Large abs/net is the finite residue version of an alternating series that would be unusable with all signs made positive.
