============================================================================================
S15 READING
============================================================================================
1. The all-positive residue and shell sums are the wrong object, just as an alternating conditionally convergent series becomes divergent when all signs are made positive.
2. The useful bound should factor into two inequalities: cusp absolute mass -> signed shell variation, then alternating shell variation -> net.
3. The persistent sequences are now visible: support floor 0..0,1; residue sign-balance by d; shell sign words; boundary count/ratio pairs; coimage null-count and max-fiber ladders.
4. LRC(14) is still open.  The next proof move is a class-by-class Dedekind/cotangent summation theorem over the non-null coimage fibers, after HYP-2616-style wall ledger deletion.
